[Event "QGD: Nc3 and Bg5"]
[LineId "qgd-nc3"]
[Main "true"]
[OpeningGroup "qgd"]
[Summary "Develop and castle, then contest the center with ...c5; attack a Pillsbury Ne5’s d4 support. In the Carlsbad (White e3/d4, Black c6/d5), watch b4-b5 and weak c6; seek active pieces and a central break."]
[Result "*"]

{[%line qgd-nc3]}
1. d4 {[%weight 30]}
d5 {Claim central space and open a diagonal for the c8 bishop. [%rules pawn-moves-two-to-six]}
2. c4 {[%weight 54]}
e6 {Support d5 and open a diagonal for the f8 bishop. [%rules pawn-moves-two-to-six]}
3. Nc3 {[%weight 44]}
Nf6 {Develop the kingside knight to prepare castling. [%rules develop-castling-side-first]}
4. Bg5 {[%weight 10]}
Be7 {Develop the bishop to prepare kingside castling; with Bd6 and White castled, ...Nxd5?? can lose the queen to Bxd8 without ...Bb4+. [%rules develop-castling-side-first]}
5. e3 {[%weight 10]}
O-O {Castle to protect the king and activate the rook. [%rules castle-early]}
6. Nf3 {[%weight 15]}
Nbd7 {Support f6 with Nd7; the Elephant trap runs cxd5 exd5 Nxd5? Nxd5 Bxd8 Bb4+ Qd2 Bxd2+ Kxd2 Kxd8, recovering the queen with check. [%rules one-move-per-piece]}
7. Rc1 {[%weight 10]}
c6 {Reinforce the central pawn on d5 before completing development. [%rules pawn-moves-two-to-six]}
8. Bd3 {[%weight 10]}
dxc4 {Release the central tension and make White spend time recapturing. [%rules capture-when-sharp]} *

